# web.public - project log.log (repo root, append-only)

Purpose: the durable narrative of what was actually done in this repo, by whom,
with evidence. Single chronological file, separated by day headers so it stays
searchable across all time. If it isn't written here with evidence, it did not
happen. Verbal "I verified it" does not count - the saved output is the proof.

Conventions:
- One entry per event, newest at the BOTTOM. Real timestamps only (time MCP).
- Day delimiter precedes each day's first entry (see format below).
- Entry format: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS | <what was done> [evidence/path or tag]
- Tag every claim: [verified] / [operator-did] / [unknown] / [blocked: reason].

